      "problem": "Express $\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt[3\\phantom{|}]{2y}}$ using power notation.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we convert the radical to a fractional exponent:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt[3\\phantom{|}]{2y}} = \\dfrac{1}{(2y)^{1/3}}\n$$\n\n \n\nThen, we take the reciprocal and convert the exponent to a negative exponent:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{(2y)^{1/3}} = (2y)^{-1/3}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{\\sqrt[3\\phantom{|}]{2y}} = (2y)^{-1/3}\n$$",
